From: TX68 Build <tx68@local>
Subject: [PATCH] tx68: honour an explicit FDT address passed to bootm

Allwinner's vendor U-Boot (v2018.05-h618) never calls boot_get_fdt() under
CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI. It hardcodes images.ft_addr to gd->fdt_blob -- U-Boot's own
control FDT, which on TX68 is the "dtb" item inside the signed TOC1
(sunxi.fex, model "sun50iw9"). The third `bootm` argument is silently ignored.

That is correct for the vendor 5.4 kernel, which expects exactly that vendor
DT. It makes booting a mainline kernel impossible: mainline Linux 6.18 came up
on the vendor Android DT, so none of its drivers matched (in particular there
is no node mainline's sunxi-mmc binds to), the eMMC never probed, and
`root=/dev/mmcblk0p1 rootwait` hung forever with no diagnostic on the console.
The giveaway in the boot log is `Machine model: sun50iw9` where our DTS says
`model = "TX68"`, plus `FDT addr: bbeccbf8` -- gd->fdt_blob relocated to
top-of-RAM, not the 0x46000000 the boot script loaded the real DTB to.

Honour an explicitly supplied FDT address (argv[2]) when there is one, exactly
as the generic non-sunxi path already does, and fall back to the control FDT
otherwise. gd->fdt_blob is untouched, so U-Boot's own drivers keep using the
vendor control FDT and the existing vendor boot flow is unaffected.
---
--- a/common/bootm.c
+++ b/common/bootm.c
@@ -294,8 +294,35 @@
 		return 1;
 	}
 #endif
-	images.ft_addr = (char *)gd->fdt_blob;
-	images.ft_len  = gd->fdt_size;
+	/*
+	 * Allwinner's original code unconditionally handed the kernel U-Boot's
+	 * own control FDT (gd->fdt_blob -- the "dtb" item inside the signed
+	 * TOC1, i.e. sunxi.fex, model "sun50iw9") and never called
+	 * boot_get_fdt() at all, so a third `bootm` argument was silently
+	 * discarded. That is fine for the vendor 5.4 kernel, which expects
+	 * exactly that vendor DT, but it makes booting a mainline kernel
+	 * impossible: mainline Linux came up on the vendor Android DT, none of
+	 * its drivers matched (no sunxi-mmc node it recognises), so the eMMC
+	 * never probed and `rootwait` hung forever with no diagnostic.
+	 *
+	 * Honour an explicitly supplied FDT address (argv[2], the third bootm
+	 * argument) when one is given, exactly as the generic non-sunxi path
+	 * below does, and fall back to the control FDT otherwise. U-Boot keeps
+	 * using the vendor control FDT for its own drivers either way --
+	 * gd->fdt_blob is not touched here -- so the existing vendor boot flow
+	 * is unaffected.
+	 */
+	if (argc > 2) {
+		ret = boot_get_fdt(flag, argc, argv, IH_ARCH_DEFAULT, &images,
+				   &images.ft_addr, &images.ft_len);
+		if (ret) {
+			puts("Could not find a valid device tree\n");
+			return 1;
+		}
+	} else {
+		images.ft_addr = (char *)gd->fdt_blob;
+		images.ft_len  = gd->fdt_size;
+	}
 	set_working_fdt_addr((ulong)images.ft_addr);
 
 	/* set this env variable for  function boot_relocate_fdt.
